From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/qcom: synchronize invalidations after releasing context halt

The context-init ASID invalidation backport waits for TLBSYNC with the
micro-MMU still halted. A fresh device boot after patch0100 times out
on both the ARM32 automatic DMA-domain attach and the later MDP domain
attach; display probing safely fails with ETIMEDOUT. This blocks testing
the physically demonstrated DSI mux fix.

The pinned MSM8226 BSP resets/invalidate/programs the bank under halt,
then resumes; its separate TLB synchronization paths run unhalted:
https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226/blob/3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256/drivers/iommu/msm_iommu-v1.c

Keep the invalidation inside the halt-protected programming sequence,
but wait for completion after enabling the programmed context and
releasing halt. Do not bypass the completion check or shorten its bound.
If completion fails, disable the context before its new page tables can
be released. Instances without the halt quirk retain the existing order.

This is a measured-failure-driven candidate; fresh boot and hardware
translation acceptance must be repeated before claiming a fix.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 25e5f299d..0e64f87ec 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -316,10 +316,10 @@ static int qcom_iommu_program_ctx(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu,
 
 	/* Drop old entries for the incoming namespace before enabling it. */
 	iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_S1_TLBIASID, ctx->pt_asid);
-	ret = qcom_iommu_ctx_tlb_sync(ctx);
-	if (ret) {
-		qcom_iommu_unhalt(qcom_iommu);
-		return ret;
+	if (!qcom_iommu->cfg || !qcom_iommu->cfg->halt) {
+		ret = qcom_iommu_ctx_tlb_sync(ctx);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 	}
 
 	/* Clear context bank fault address fault status registers */
@@ -347,6 +347,16 @@ static int qcom_iommu_program_ctx(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu,
 	/* SCTLR */
 	iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR, ctx->sctlr);
 	qcom_iommu_unhalt(qcom_iommu);
+	/* The halted front-end must run before an invalidation can complete. */
+	if (qcom_iommu->cfg && qcom_iommu->cfg->halt) {
+		ret = qcom_iommu_ctx_tlb_sync(ctx);
+		if (ret) {
+			/* Do not leave a walker referencing a failed domain's tables. */
+			iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR, 0);
+			wmb(); /* Disable the walker before its tables are released. */
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
 	return 0;
 }
 
